workedExamples.question_text:
Concrete contains cement, sand and gravel in the ratio $1:2:3$.
(a) How much of each ingredient is in a $42$ kg batch?
(b) A separate batch uses $9$ kg of cement. How much concrete can be made in total?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\node[anchor=east] at (-0.2,2.3) {Cement};
\node[anchor=east] at (-0.2,1.3) {Sand};
\node[anchor=east] at (-0.2,0.3) {Gravel};
\draw (0,2) rectangle (1,2.6);
\draw (0,1) rectangle (2,1.6);
\draw (1,1)--(1,1.6);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3,0.6);
\draw (1,0)--(1,0.6);
\draw (2,0)--(2,0.6);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

